      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Dickerson Mine, owned by New Jersey’s 7th Governor Mahlon Dickerson, supplied iron for the Revolutionary War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mine_Hill_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Today, old railway beds and foundations echo Mine Hill’s powerful 19th‑century iron industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.educationmagz.blog/mine-hill-nj-county-guide-morris-facts",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Morris County, where Mine Hill sits, blends suburban density with preserved natural spaces and a 19th‑century iron legacy.",
